# The OAK-D Pro's USB 3 link drops because of USB 3 Link Power Management.
#
# Measured on the Jetson, boot of 3 Nov 2026, with kernel timestamps:
#
#   09:34:31  usb 2-1.2: Disable of device-initiated U1 failed.
#   09:34:31  usb 2-1.2: Disable of device-initiated U2 failed.
#   09:34:32  usb 2-1.2: USB disconnect, device number 3
#   09:34:33  usb 1-2.2: new high-speed USB device number 6
#   09:34:35  usb 1-2.2: USB disconnect, device number 6
#   09:34:36  usb 2-1.2: new SuperSpeed USB device number 4
#   09:34:36  usb 2-1.2: USB disconnect, device number 4
#   ... and on, alternating SuperSpeed and high-speed
#
# The same pattern sits in the 20 Oct log, and one of these disconnects is
# at 09:14:10 - inside flight 00000118. Every one of them reaches our node
# as "RuntimeError: Device already closed or disconnected: Input/output
# error" from startPipeline, 145 of those across the recorded runs. In
# flight 00000117 it took the VPS out altogether: GPS2 managed 42 packets,
# all of them fix status 1, so the aircraft flew that whole flight with no
# vision aiding at all.
#
# U1 and U2 are the link's low-power states. The device fails to leave them
# on demand, so the link is torn down and re-enumerated. Keeping the link
# out of them costs no bandwidth, which matters because this camera needs
# USB 3: two 800p mono streams at 25 fps is about 410 Mbit/s and USB 2 tops
# out near 400, so dropping to high-speed would starve the flow instead.
#
# 03e7:f63b is the booted Movidius VPU; 03e7:2485 is the same camera in its
# bootloader state, before depthai flashes it, and both are matched so the
# setting is in place before the pipeline opens.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 644 etc/99-oakd-no-usb3-lpm.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="03e7", ATTR{idProduct}=="f63b", \
  TEST=="power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u1", ATTR{power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u1}="0"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="03e7", ATTR{idProduct}=="f63b", \
  TEST=="power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u2", ATTR{power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u2}="0"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="03e7", ATTR{idProduct}=="2485", \
  TEST=="power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u1", ATTR{power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u1}="0"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="03e7", ATTR{idProduct}=="2485", \
  TEST=="power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u2", ATTR{power/usb3_hardware_lpm_u2}="0"
